yo what is up everybody mad luigi here  and today i want to talk about something  i mentioned in my last video on the lore  of radon a good number of people in the  comments expressed contention with the  idea i presented that radon was acting  on ronnie's side so i want to spend a  little time looking solely at that and  presenting my theory in more detail i  think a closer examination will reveal  an even stronger case of an affable  relationship between the mightiest  demigod and his older sister  one of the main things i saw in many of  the comments that was used as evidence  of radon acting against ronnie was the  supposed fact that radon loved the  golden order which i think is  unsupported the idea goes that because  radon glorified his father to some  extent but really godfrey first elden  lord and the golden lion of the order  then radon also glorified the golden  order itself but this misses the point  of radon's affinity for godfrey verdan  is shown many times to take pride in  battle and war he liked the heroic  implications of the red hair he  inherited from his father and saw  himself as following in the footsteps of  godfrey in being the lord of the  battlefields lion  these idealizations show radon soying  out not over the order despite his  father and godfrey's strong connections  to it but to the glory of two god tier  warriors  radon seeks out and enjoys battle he has  never shown prioritizing something  related to the order over this theme and  if he is the one fighting morgot in the  opening slide then we have an example of  radon essentially going against the  order or what's left of it at least by  attacking the capital city this  connection may be tenuous as the golden  order was in shambles after the  shattering but at the least it certainly  does not lend credit to the idea that  radon was a big follower or fanatic of  the order  another piece of evidence against my  theory of team radon ronnie is the  description of the telescope which  states  during the age of the erd tree carrion  astrology withered on the vine the fate  once writ in the night skies had been  fettered by the golden order  this could be read as radon acting as an  agent of the order by holding back the  stars and halting any carrying fate but  i think that's a weak reading verdan  himself was part of the carrion line and  practiced space-based sorcery it is  unlikely that he would actively wither  away this tradition and source of power  yes he uses the gravity sorcery of the  alabaster lords and not the morkarian  glinstone magic but his love of battle  still makes me think that this is  unlikely plus taking both sentences of  the description together makes me think  this is a more broad point of lore  instead of being about radon holding  back the stars i'm inclined to read this  as the influence of the earth tree  pushing out the influence of anything  else such as the stars which the  carrions had studied and drawn power  from since before the earth tree's age  this seems to tie into the broader theme  of er tree supremacy by the order as  opposed to the single actions of one  demigod who isn't even a confirmed  follower of the order  and this video isn't just going to be me  on the back foot there's some more  context that didn't make it into my  radon video that i think supports the  idea of radon and ronnie having some  amicable understanding a lot of this  comes from the connection between their  second and commands blacksmith eg for  ronnie and witch hunter jaron for radon  eg is ronnie's war counsellor and used  to serve carrion royals  jaren used to be a wanderer before  spending time as a guest of the carrion  royals and then becoming radon's guest  commander  we see the carrion tie which makes sense  as both ronnie and radan would have  spent their youths in the carrying court  but further than this is their dialogue  both of them have words about the other  when asked jaren says well  i haven't heard that name in an age  then you must serve princess ronnie  the next time you speak to eg  tell him this  the festival of radon will surely set  rani's fate back into motion  bye-bye  is that old fool still hammering out  weapons  is enormous frame cramped in that little  place  bit of a haughty sword  strange fella when i knew him  and funny thing  his swords were all blunt as stone  but not one of them decayed when faced  with a scarlet rot  here we learned two important facts  first jaron is giving advice to eg about  how to help ronnie move forward by  killing radon in the festival  second is that despite jeering at them  jaren commends eg's weapons and reveals  that they were used by radon's army the  mention of scarlet rot references the  battle of radon and melania along with  their forces eg made some if not all of  the weapons that radon's army fought  melania with this is a large indication  of trust and allyship if anything was eg  was a core component of radon's armed  forces highlighting a link between  ronnie's side and radons and i think  this casts doubt on a notion i saw  people making in comments previously  that ronnie coordinated with melania to  attack radon why would she coordinate  and attack and then supply the other  side with arms yes ronnie could be a  giga chad manipulator making everybody  else fight each other and sowing chaos  but then we are really stretching to  make a conspiracy fit we don't have any  further direct or indirect evidence of  this kind of thing what we know for  certain is that ronnie aided radon in a  big way jaren is thankful for this aid  and wants to help ronnie his mentioning  of how to progress her fate indicates  some level of radon's holding back the  stars not having a huge goal of stopping  ronnie jaren is bound and wants to give  radon a good warrior's death and is  happy to help perrani at the same time  if rudon was holding back the stars to  get in ronnie's way then jaron likely  wouldn't be so forthcoming with  information which would aid ronnie here  he is clearly showing himself to be  somewhat at least on ronnie's side so a  natural follow-up would be that radon  was also on ronnie's side or at least  wasn't actively trying to mess with her  or her plans  so that's jaren's side if we head over  to eg we can hear him say jaren  now that's a name i haven't heard for a  while  before taking up the banner of general  radan  he was a guest of the karyan royal  family  an expert swordsman to be sure  but ever  eccentric  no surprise he'd get wrapped up in some  festival  oh no  wait  how did i not see it before  i ought to retire as war counsellor for  such a gross oversight  let me explain  the fate of the karyan royal family is  guided by the stars  as is the fate of lady rani  first air in the karyan royal line  but general radha is the conqueror of  the stars  who stood up to the swirling  constellations halting their movement in  a smashing victory  and so if general radan were defeated  the stars would once again resume their  movement  as would lady rani's destiny  perhaps  even revealing the elusive path  that leads to knock wrong  so eg rambles a bit more and doesn't  give as juicy of extra lore but his  words are still important because they  highlight how eg as war counselor  doesn't make any sort of insinuation  about radon acting against ronnie  through his star stopping he even goes  so far as to call it a smashing victory  which isn't necessarily positive but  basically sounds like eg is  congratulating radon for such an  impressive feat if it was clear that  radon was doing this to spite ronnie  then it doesn't seem likely that eg  would ignore that and go on to basically  commend radon  from these connections it gets pretty  hard to paint a picture of radon  intentionally acting against irani the  bond between their forces suggests that  they are on good terms or were their  most recent interaction radon's halting  of the stars seems like a grand feat  with at worst neutral implications in  how it impacts others at least by the  intention  perhaps no one knew what impact this  stellar battle would have but we can say  at least with a moderate amount of  certainty that it was not done with the  intention of spiting ronnie radon likely  just saw it as a grand avenue for battle  as there weren't too many big battles  left to be had after the time of  godfreak and because he did it when he  was young it would have been hard for  radon to then later on go get help from  eg when fighting melania if the star  conquest did intentionally mess with  eg's master's plan  now yes the eg weapon reference could be  explained in that eg made weapons for  radon's forces long ago and they just  happened to be rot resistant but the  strong theme of camaraderie and bond  between eg and jiren would imply that it  would be more reasonable to read the  situation as eg providing aid in that  more recent conflict the themes and  subtext and even explicit text really  point to eg and jiren being on good  terms and wanting to help each other and  to some degree each other's masters we  see that explicitly with jaren helping  ronnie  and such a positive bond between  sub-commanders while it could happen  with the main commanders budding heads i  don't see any reason to believe that  they're not representative of a positive  relationship between their commanders so  with all of that presented i think  ronnie and radon are very likely chill  with each other if not working together  in some degree so what do you think is  my lore theory convincing let me know in  the comments your thoughts on the matter  and any of these other pieces of lore  today i just wanted to delve a little  bit more into this so that will be it  for this video i hope you enjoyed and  make sure to subscribe if you want to  see more videos like this on eldon ring  lore game analysis and more thanks for  watching peace  also just one more example of vg and  jaren bean bros which supports ronnie  and radon being chill after we defeat  radon eg will say now the festival is  over  and general radhan is defeated  jeren's duties are finally fulfilled  though we served different masters  i could see he was truly adept in his  role  now the time has come to remind him of  an old promise made  with the stars of fate set into motion  a certain sorceress is dispossessed of  her immortality  finally  we can be rid of a long-standing carrion  weed  eg is talking about selen here who we  see jiren want to kill and who he can  help jiren kill or defend from jaren  regardless of where they stand with  selen this is another point of  connection between the two second in  commands jaron and eg seem to have quite  the number of ties between them and i  think this really makes the case that  their leaders ronnie and radon are on  pretty okay terms

